    'faqs' => [
        ['Which visa do I need to study MBBS in China?', 'The X1 visa. According to Chinese embassy visa instructions, checked November 2026, X1 is issued for study in China of more than 180 days and X2 for study of no more than 180 days. The MBBS lasts six years, so MBBS students apply for X1.'],
        ['What is the JW202 form?', 'It is the form titled Visa Application for Study in China, issued for your admission and sent to you with the admission letter. Embassies ask for the JW201 or JW202 together with the admission letter when you apply for an X1 visa. At XJMU the JW202 visa letter is included in the first-year package.'],
        ['When does XJMU issue the admission letter and JW202?', 'After the Pre-Admission Letter and the ¥2,000 seat reservation deposit. The admission letter and JW202 form are issued after review, which takes two to four weeks.'],
        ['How much bank statement is required for a China student visa?', 'It depends on the embassy, and websites quote conflicting amounts. For Pakistan, the Karachi visa centre\'s X1 page (dated 24 August 2026) asks for scholarship evidence or proof of US$2,500 per academic year, with a closing balance enough for the whole period of study. For other countries, check your own embassy.'],
        ['How long does a China student visa take from Pakistan?', 'The Karachi visa centre\'s page says it generally needs four working days and offers no fast service, and that requests for more documents take longer. X1 applicants must also attend an interview in person. Check your centre\'s current notice. Do not book a flight until the visa is in your passport.'],
        ['What is the China student visa fee?', 'Visa fees differ by nationality, country and number of entries, and they change, so we do not print one. Check the fee table of your own embassy or visa centre. At XJMU the first-year package includes the student visa item listed by the university.'],
        ['Do I need a residence permit after I arrive?', 'Yes. According to Chinese embassy visa instructions, checked November 2026, X1 visa holders must apply for a residence permit at the local exit and entry administration within 30 days of entering China. The international student office at XJMU helps with the application.'],
        ['How much does the residence permit cost each year?', 'XJMU lists ¥800 a year for the residence permit and ¥350 for the physical examination from the second year, inside the yearly total of about ¥35,950. In the first year these items are part of the ¥49,950 package.'],
        ['Is the seat deposit refunded if my visa letter is rejected?', 'The ¥2,000 seat reservation deposit is refunded if the JW202 visa letter is rejected. The ¥1,000 application fee is non-refundable once the Pre-Admission Letter is issued. Ask admissions in writing what applies in any other case.'],
        ['Can XJMU or an agent guarantee my visa?', 'No. The consular officer decides whether to issue a visa and may ask for more documents. The university provides the admission letter and JW202 form. A complete and truthful application is the best preparation you can make.'],
    ],
    'related' => ['mbbs-in-china-spring-intake-2027', 'mbbs-in-china-fees-2027', 'life-in-urumqi-for-international-students'],
];
